          "rule_id": "proofline:PY-MUTATE-MAPPING-DURING-ITERATION",
          "cwe_id": null,
          "title": "Deleting entries while iterating raises at runtime",
          "explanation": "The change replaces iteration over a snapshot of the keys with iteration over the live mapping. For a normal Python dict, deleting a key in the loop changes its size and causes the iterator to raise `RuntimeError: dictionary changed size during iteration`. The prior `list(values)` avoided this by materializing the keys before mutation.",
          "user_impact": "`prune` fails partway through instead of removing all `None`-valued entries, and the input may be left partially modified.",
          "severity": "high",
          "primary_location": {
            "path": "src/module.py",
            "start_line": 2,
            "end_line": 4,
            "side": "head",
            "commit_sha": "d5094d23f97fa2c4eedebb89998830bdc5c1d788",
            "snippet": "for key in values:\n    if values[key] is None:\n        del values[key]"
          },
